Conversation "1" -- "2" ConversationParticipant : authorised participants
UserAccount "1" -- "0..*" ConversationParticipant : membership [logical ID]
Conversation "1" -- "0..*" Message : messages
ConversationParticipant "1" -- "0..*" Message : authorised sender
Listing "0..1" -- "0..*" Conversation : listing context [logical ID]
MatchDecision "0..1" -- "0..*" Conversation : pair context [logical ID]

note bottom of CampusIdentityLink
  Provider + Subject uniquely identify one local account.
  Campus sign-in is beyond the semester scope.
end note
note bottom of AccountRole
  Future Moderator and Campus Benefits Manager permissions.
  A person retains one account; these are not account subclasses.
end note
note bottom of NotificationDelivery
  Event + recipient + channel suppress duplicates.
  Delivery failure does not undo the originating business event.
  One current preference per user/channel.
end note
note bottom of BenefitRedemption
  Each redemption refers to exactly one benefit rule version.
  Eligibility reads authoritative credibility; it does not alter
  the ledger without a separately approved spending rule.
end note
note bottom of Conversation
  Context: exactly one listing OR one accepted pair {xor}.
  Initial future scope: exactly two distinct account participants.
  A message's sender membership belongs to the same conversation.
  Unrelated users cannot access it by knowing its identifier.
end note
!endif

legend bottom
  <<Existing>>: current Auth domain classes; selected members shown.
  <<Semester>>: proposed semester domain classes and responsibilities.
  <<Calculated>>: proposed calculated view; persistence not implied.
  <<Future>>: beyond this semester; module deployment boundaries undecided.
  Associations show domain relationships, not automatic navigation or API access.
  Associations crossing ownership boundaries use logical IDs, never database FKs.
  Operations on planned classes are conceptual responsibilities, not existing APIs.
  Selected fields only; identity/link details of future records remain to be refined.
endlegend
@enduml
